  "cli_result_text": "Submitted the file set required for the dependency-graph impact analysis linking Log4j2's bridge-module restructuring (`log4j-to-slf4j`, `log4j-slf4j-impl`, `log4j-slf4j2-impl`, `log4j-spring-boot`) to Spring Boot's logging auto-configuration (`LoggingSystem`, `LoggingSystemFactory`, `Log4J2LoggingSystem`, `LoggingApplicationListener`), most important first:\n\n- `Log4J2LoggingSystem.java` and its `Factory` (detects Log4j2 via `Log4jContextFactory` presence) \u2014 the core detection logic Spring Boot uses.\n- `LoggingSystem.java` / `LoggingSystemFactory.java` \u2014 the abstraction and `spring.factories`-driven discovery mechanism.\n- `spring.factories` (spring-boot core) \u2014 declares the ordered list of `LoggingSystemFactory` implementations (Logback \u2192 Log4j2 \u2192 JUL).\n- `LoggingApplicationListener.java` \u2014 where `LoggingSystem.get()` is invoked during Spring Boot startup.\n- `spring-boot-starter-log4j2/build.gradle` \u2014 pulls in `log4j-slf4j2-impl` + `log4j-core` + `log4j-jul`, showing the intended bridge combination.\n- `log4j-to-slf4j/pom.xml` and `SLF4JLoggerContextFactory.java` \u2014 the Log4j-API\u2192SLF4J bridge module (opposite direction from `log4j-slf4j-impl`), whose presence is mutually exclusive with the SLF4J-to-Log4j adapters.\n- `Log4j2SpringBootLoggingSystem.java` (from `log4j-spring-boot`) and its `spring.factories` \u2014 a third-party override `LoggingSystemFactory` with `@Order(0)` (higher precedence than core's `LOWEST_PRECEDENCE`), which competes with core Spring Boot's own Log4J2LoggingSystem.Factory.\n- `log4j-bom/pom.xml`, `log4j-slf4j-impl/pom.xml`, `log4j-slf4j2-impl/pom.xml` \u2014 version-management and mutual-exclusion declarations across the SLF4J 1.x vs 2.x bridge split.\n- `Log4jLoggerFactory.java` (log4j-slf4j-impl) \u2014 runtime guard throwing `LoggingException` if `log4j-to-slf4j` is also on the classpath.\n- `RELEASE-NOTES.md` \u2014 documents the SLF4J-binding break that produced the `log4j-slf4j-impl` vs `log4j-slf4j18-impl`/`log4j-slf4j2-impl` split.\n- `logging.adoc` (spring-boot-docs) \u2014 documents the official migration path between `spring-boot-starter-logging` and `spring-boot-starter-log4j2`.",
